Lebanese President Joseph Aoun is urging the judiciary to issue a long-awaited indictment over the 2020 Beirut port blast, as the country marks six years since the catastrophe which killed over 200 people.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/f99f4238-d6e2-11ea-a516-005056bf87d6/w:1024/p:16x9/2020-08-05t052637z_876238970_rc2h7i9tqddc_rtrmadp_3_lebanon-security-blast_0.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/f99f4238-d6e2-11ea-a516-005056bf87d6/w:1024/p:16x9/2020-08-05t052637z_876238970_rc2h7i9tqddc_rtrmadp_3_lebanon-security-blast_0.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ba5814ec-8f4b-11f1-9216-efe0ac09f616</guid><pubDate>Tue, 04 Aug 2026 05:46:30 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/f99f4238-d6e2-11ea-a516-005056bf87d6/w:1024/p:16x9/2020-08-05t052637z_876238970_rc2h7i9tqddc_rtrmadp_3_lebanon-security-blast_0.jpg">REUTERS/Mohamed Azakir</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>EU steps up AI regulation as new transparency rules come into effect</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260803-eu-steps-up-ai-regulation-as-new-transparency-rules-come-into-effect</link><description>
The European Union is stepping up its oversight of artificial intelligence this week, as the main provisions of its landmark AI Act became applicable, giving regulators stronger powers to inspect advanced models and sanction companies that break the rules.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/5057dac8-8f3c-11f1-a171-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-36RU8KY.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/5057dac8-8f3c-11f1-a171-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-36RU8KY.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d68ac5ba-8f0f-11f1-b557-fda0ec721e5e</guid><pubDate>Mon, 03 Aug 2026 16:06:09 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/5057dac8-8f3c-11f1-a171-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-36RU8KY.jpg">AFP - KIRILL KUDRYAVTSEV</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Ghana bets on AI and coding to modernise basic education</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260804-ghana-bets-on-ai-and-coding-to-modernise-basic-education-africa-technology</link><description>
Ghana has introduced artificial intelligence, coding and computer programming into its national curriculum, for pupils from kindergarten to junior high school, becoming one of the few African countries to embed these subjects in basic education.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c4eebdc2-8cc4-11f1-a382-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/Picture-3-7.jpeg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c4eebdc2-8cc4-11f1-a382-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/Picture-3-7.jpeg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">dc6d6782-8cc4-11f1-b4ed-dd19f77b313a</guid><pubDate>Tue, 04 Aug 2026 09:01:49 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c4eebdc2-8cc4-11f1-a382-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/Picture-3-7.jpeg">© Michael Sarpong Mfum</source><dc:creator>Michael Sarpong Mfum in Ghana</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>EU ministers set to meet over migrant crossings in Ceuta</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260803-eu-ministers-set-to-meet-over-migrant-crossings-in-ceuta</link><description>
The European Union will hold an emergency video conference meeting of national ministers on Tuesday to discuss the mass migrant crossings into Spain's North African enclave of Ceuta.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/4a8ffb0e-8f03-11f1-b586-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C3RV2BZ.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/4a8ffb0e-8f03-11f1-b586-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C3RV2BZ.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e1f76250-8eab-11f1-b0dc-27f4398d8a9e</guid><pubDate>Mon, 03 Aug 2026 06:16:30 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/4a8ffb0e-8f03-11f1-b586-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C3RV2BZ.jpg">AFP - HENRY NICHOLLS</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>French wildfires expose buried WWII shells</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260803-french-wildfires-expose-buried-wwii-shells-gironde-bordeaux</link><description>
Devastating wildfires in the southwest of France have uncovered a hidden cache of Second World War-era shells in the village of Le Porge, adding an explosive edge to an already dangerous situation. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/03b403a0-8f31-11f1-a3ef-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C3U66TE.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/03b403a0-8f31-11f1-a3ef-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C3U66TE.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a62a351e-8f31-11f1-ad8f-35df43690abf</guid><pubDate>Mon, 03 Aug 2026 15:04:02 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/03b403a0-8f31-11f1-a3ef-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C3U66TE.jpg">© AFP - ROMAIN PERROCHEAU</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Deadly helicopter crash in Greece exposes growing danger of Europe’s wildfires</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260803-deadly-helicopter-crash-in-greece-exposes-growing-danger-of-europe-s-wildfires</link><description>
Water-bombing aircraft returned to the skies over Greece on Monday as firefighters battled several major blazes near Athens, a day after two pilots were killed when their fire-fighting helicopter collided with another aircraft.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/7baa6236-8f2d-11f1-9e22-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C3RT8T6.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/7baa6236-8f2d-11f1-9e22-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C3RT8T6.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">338b491a-8f10-11f1-b4a3-539eb0546072</guid><pubDate>Mon, 03 Aug 2026 13:16:03 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/7baa6236-8f2d-11f1-9e22-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C3RT8T6.jpg">AFP - ANGELOS TZORTZINIS</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Cameroon government says President Biya's prolonged absence no cause for concern</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260803-cameroon-government-says-president-biya-s-prolonged-absence-no-cause-for-concern</link><description>
President Paul Biya left Cameroon in early June for what his office described as a "short private stay in Europe." Addressing the concerns regarding this prolonged absence, a government spokesperson has told RFI the 93-year-old head of state is healthy and hard at work, even while abroad. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/46322daa-8ef1-11f1-92ec-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-A7X96PA.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/46322daa-8ef1-11f1-92ec-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-A7X96PA.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">43f082b6-8f29-11f1-a565-b12c1aa1cb82</guid><pubDate>Mon, 03 Aug 2026 13:58:32 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/46322daa-8ef1-11f1-92ec-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-A7X96PA.jpg">AFP - ALBERTO PIZZOLI</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>French court rejects pro-Kremlin commentator's deportation appeal</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260803-french-court-rejects-pro-kremlin-commentator-s-deportation-appeal</link><description>
A Paris court on Monday rejected an appeal by a Russian television commentator against an order to leave France after authorities accused her of spreading pro-Kremlin propaganda. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/62042cca-6031-11f1-9bbe-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/KF-Cnews-2.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/62042cca-6031-11f1-9bbe-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/KF-Cnews-2.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ad3b04d0-8f29-11f1-a683-ed1e659f4e53</guid><pubDate>Mon, 03 Aug 2026 11:09:03 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/62042cca-6031-11f1-9bbe-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/KF-Cnews-2.jpg">© screenshot Youtube</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Wildfire threat eases across France despite heat alerts and storm warnings</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260803-wildfire-threat-eases-across-france-despite-heat-alerts-and-storm-warnings</link><description>
France’s wildfire situation has shown signs of improvement on Monday, with thousands of residents and tourists preparing to return to evacuated areas in the south-west, even as firefighters remained on alert amid high temperatures, low humidity and a new risk of violent thunderstorms.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/dc8324a8-8f14-11f1-85fb-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C3RB2NX.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/dc8324a8-8f14-11f1-85fb-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C3RB2NX.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f5a933dc-8f0f-11f1-af09-fda0ec721e5e</guid><pubDate>Mon, 03 Aug 2026 09:37:08 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/dc8324a8-8f14-11f1-85fb-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C3RB2NX.jpg">AFP - ROMAIN PERROCHEAU</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Hundreds flee Ethiopia to war-torn Sudan following new fighting in Tigray</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260803-hundreds-flee-ethiopia-to-war-torn-sudan-following-new-fighting-in-tigray</link><description>
In Ethiopia, hundreds of people have started to flee to Sudan following Saturday's fighting, when clashes in Tigray pitted federal forces against rebels from the Tigray People's Liberation Front (TPLF). Both sides accuse each other of seeking to trigger a new conflict. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a6327e60-8f20-11f1-a0a4-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/tigray-2026-afp-000-A26B6PB.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a6327e60-8f20-11f1-a0a4-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/tigray-2026-afp-000-A26B6PB.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b34f8102-8f1f-11f1-90aa-db88ccb4d9a8</guid><pubDate>Mon, 03 Aug 2026 12:01:13 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a6327e60-8f20-11f1-a0a4-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/tigray-2026-afp-000-A26B6PB.jpg">AFP - ABEL GEREZGIHER</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Sudan army's drone attack on court kills 35 in Darfur: NGO</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260803-sudan-army-s-drone-attack-on-court-kills-35-in-darfur-ngo</link><description>
A Sudanese rights group reported that the Sudanese army (SAF) struck a traditional court in a Rapid Support Forces-held village in North Darfur with drones on Sunday, killing 35 people.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/556b7ef0-374b-11f1-9147-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-824J2WE-1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/556b7ef0-374b-11f1-9147-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-824J2WE-1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9e8adaec-8f19-11f1-97a7-458f4247222d</guid><pubDate>Mon, 03 Aug 2026 09:56:01 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/556b7ef0-374b-11f1-9147-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-824J2WE-1.jpg">© AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Benin’s new Senate raises questions over power and legitimacy</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260803-benin-s-new-senate-raises-questions-over-power-and-legitimacy</link><description>
Benin’s new senate was inaugurated in Porto-Novo last week, creating a second chamber of parliament with powers to review legislation, protect constitutional rules and discipline political figures.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/fcfc79a8-d44a-11f0-b461-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2025-12-08T110950Z-9433312-RC29CIAHRLSM-RTRMADP-3-BENIN-SECURITY.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/fcfc79a8-d44a-11f0-b461-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2025-12-08T110950Z-9433312-RC29CIAHRLSM-RTRMADP-3-BENIN-SECURITY.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3a265bb6-8bf5-11f1-a2cf-377d54a72fad</guid><pubDate>Mon, 03 Aug 2026 13:32:26 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/fcfc79a8-d44a-11f0-b461-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2025-12-08T110950Z-9433312-RC29CIAHRLSM-RTRMADP-3-BENIN-SECURITY.jpg">REUTERS - Charles Placide Tossou</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>France tightens checks on foreign investment amid concerns over national security</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260803-france-tightens-checks-on-foreign-investment-amid-concerns-over-national-security</link><description>
France is strengthening its oversight of non-European investment in strategically important companies, lowering the threshold at which foreign share purchases require government approval.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/dd3aabce-8f09-11f1-8052-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C2UL24Z.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/dd3aabce-8f09-11f1-8052-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C2UL24Z.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ad56355e-8f09-11f1-860b-fda0ec721e5e</guid><pubDate>Mon, 03 Aug 2026 07:23:55 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/dd3aabce-8f09-11f1-8052-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C2UL24Z.jpg">AFP - DIMITAR DILKOFF</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Why one American expert would be happy to see fewer US military bases in Europe</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260802-why-one-american-expert-would-be-happy-to-see-fewer-us-military-bases-in-europe</link><description>
As Washington begins its review of the United States' military presence in Europe – confirmed this week by Under Secretary of War, Elbridge Colby – few observers welcome the prospect more than David Vine, a long-time critic of the sprawling network of American overseas bases.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/ad321b48-af66-11f0-b2e0-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/Allemagne-Etats-Unis-Ramstein.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/ad321b48-af66-11f0-b2e0-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/Allemagne-Etats-Unis-Ramstein.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">404eb5d0-8c16-11f1-9756-1d72cbe21a0f</guid><pubDate>Sun, 02 Aug 2026 19:11:44 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/ad321b48-af66-11f0-b2e0-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/Allemagne-Etats-Unis-Ramstein.jpg">AFP - KIRILL KUDRYAVTSEV</source><dc:creator>Jan van der Made</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>UN chief proposes fresh talks to Cyprus leaders, aiming to end 'frozen conflict'</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260802-un-chief-proposes-fresh-talks-to-cyprus-leaders-aiming-to-end-frozen-conflict</link><description>
United Nations chief Antonio Guterres travelled to Cyprus this week with an offer of new peace talks – the latest attempt to resolve a conflict that has outlasted 11 of his predecessors. The island's division, sealed by Turkey's 1974 invasion but rooted in the flawed power-sharing constitution of 1960, is one of the world's longest-lasting frozen conflicts.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/33498b20-8b59-11f1-8972-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C3FL36M.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/33498b20-8b59-11f1-8972-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C3FL36M.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9e4ce246-8b59-11f1-a4b1-a54c6b50e563</guid><pubDate>Sun, 02 Aug 2026 12:12:32 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/33498b20-8b59-11f1-8972-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C3FL36M.jpg">AFP - PETROS KARADJIAS</source><dc:creator>Jan van der Made</dc:creator></item><item><category>Science and Technology</category><title>Astronomers find clear evidence that Betelgeuse star 'is not single'</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/science-and-technology/20260802-astronomers-find-clear-evidence-that-betelgeuse-star-is-not-single</link><description>
Astronomers have this week unveiled the first image of an elusive companion star orbiting Betelgeuse, one of the brightest and best-known stars located in the Orion constellation.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/ecb49f30-8a84-11f1-821d-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/Betelgeuse.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/ecb49f30-8a84-11f1-821d-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/Betelgeuse.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">25245c68-8a83-11f1-8da0-6555508abb97</guid><pubDate>Sun, 02 Aug 2026 14:20:49 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/ecb49f30-8a84-11f1-821d-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/Betelgeuse.jpg">© ESO/Digitized Sky Survey 2. Acknowledgment: Davide De Martin.</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Environment</category><title>Heatwaves to increase 'fivefold by 2050', warns French weather bureau chief</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/environment/20260802-heatwaves-to-increase-fivefold-by-2050-warns-french-weather-bureau-chief</link><description>
"We have had more heatwaves in the last 15 years than during the previous 60 years," the CEO of France's weather bureau Météo-France, Virginie Schwarz said on Thursday. As France experiences its fourth heatwave of the summer, experts warn preventative measures to deal with the changing climate are severely lacking. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/041ec91c-8c0f-11f1-abb4-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-29T173908Z-1838555039-RC2SNMA1KHAO-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-WEATHER-FRANCE-WILDFIRE.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/041ec91c-8c0f-11f1-abb4-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-29T173908Z-1838555039-RC2SNMA1KHAO-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-WEATHER-FRANCE-WILDFIRE.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">bd7a2b72-8c05-11f1-9d12-e58b7addb2db</guid><pubDate>Sun, 02 Aug 2026 09:37:03 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/041ec91c-8c0f-11f1-abb4-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-29T173908Z-1838555039-RC2SNMA1KHAO-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-WEATHER-FRANCE-WILDFIRE.jpg">REUTERS - Yves Herman</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sports</category><title>Wiebes triumphs again to set stage win record at Women's Tour de France</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/sports/20260802-wiebes-triumphs-again-to-set-stage-win-record-at-women-s-tour-de-france</link><description>
Lorena Wiebes from the Netherlands won her second consecutive stage at the 2026 Women's Tour de France on Sunday to set a record of seven stage victories in the five-year-old race.
